Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2020 02:20:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] initialize peercount

gcc on several platforms complains about this. It might not be a problem
but it's not clear from the state machine.
---
 src/usr.sbin/ntpd/ntp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/usr.sbin/ntpd/ntp.c b/src/usr.sbin/ntpd/ntp.c
index b2c70cf6f..9e72f14d3 100644
--- a/src/usr.sbin/ntpd/ntp.c
+++ b/src/usr.sbin/ntpd/ntp.c
@@ -555,7 +555,7 @@ ntp_dispatch_imsg_dns(void)
 	u_int16_t		 dlen;
 	u_char			*p;
 	struct ntp_addr		*h;
-	size_t			 addrcount, peercount, excount;
+	size_t			 addrcount, peercount = 0, excount;
 	int			 n, probe;
 
 	if (imsgbuf_read(ibuf_dns) != 1)
